    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes along with the full build. \n\nThe change is complete. Here's what I implemented for the `capacityWarning` feature:\n\n1. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 In `addOwner`, after the existing hard-rejection check (`ownersInCity >= 50` still throws `CityAtCapacityException`, unchanged), added `boolean capacityWarning = ownersInCity >= 40;` and set it on the owner via `owner.setCapacityWarning(capacityWarning)`. Since execution only reaches this point when `ownersInCity < 50`, the flag is true exactly for the 40\u201349 range.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added the `capacityWarning` field (`@Column(name = \"capacity_warning\")`) with getter/setter, mirroring `bulkSignupWarning`.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added the `capacityWarning` boolean `readOnly` property to the owner schema, so the OpenAPI-generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct maps it by name into the JSON response.\n\n4. **Schema files** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 Added the `capacity_warning BOOLEAN` column, required because tests run with `ddl-auto=none`.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreWarnsWhenApproachingCapacity` and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
